# Everything a keeper build is given (#2651): CI exports exactly these paths
# of the commit it builds, and nothing else, to build.sh
# (.github/workflows/keeper-host-release.yml). So two commits whose export of
# these paths is byte-identical build the same bundle; CI publishes it under
# that export's digest (build-source.sh), and the keeper machine deploys a
# commit only when its digest differs from the running release's. A path the
# build needs and this list leaves out makes the build fail, never pass on
# stale input.
#
# The root manifests decide what pnpm installs, and with which pnpm.
package.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
# The keeper and the workspace packages it depends on, devDependencies
# included (`pnpm install --filter '@vaipakam/keeper...'` installs them all).
apps/keeper
packages/anvil-harness
packages/contracts
packages/lib
packages/push
# Indexer modules the keeper bundles by relative import
# (scripts/lib/keeper-databases.mjs reads the private-database list there).
apps/indexer/scripts/lib
